1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,570
You woke up this morning, and before your feet touched the floor, your mind had already made a list.

2
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:07,400
Not a list of what you have.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,390
A list of what is still missing.

4
00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:11,580
The conversation you are dreading.

5
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:13,690
The thing that has still not changed.

6
00:00:13,690 --> 00:00:16,750
And underneath it all, a quieter thought.

7
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:18,620
I know I should be thankful.

8
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,610
I just do not feel it today.

9
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:22,360
And that feels like guilt.

10
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:26,350
So before the day asks anything of you, let us set that list down.

11
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:27,910
Just for a few minutes.

12
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:29,660
You can pick it up again later.

13
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:31,230
Take one slow breath.

14
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:34,970
And instead of holding your hands closed, open them.

15
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,150
There is a line in the saddest book in the Bible.

16
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:42,650
Lamentations chapter three, verses twenty-two and twenty-three.

17
00:00:42,650 --> 00:00:47,970
Because of the Lord's great love we are not consumed, for his compassions never fail.

18
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:49,600
They are new every morning.

19
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,190
Great is your faithfulness.

20
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:52,990
Notice the word new.

21
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:54,200
Not leftover.

22
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:57,740
Not what remained after yesterday used up its share.

23
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:58,610
New.

24
00:00:58,610 --> 00:01:04,920
Whatever you spent yesterday, this morning has its own supply, and it was here before you woke.

25
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:08,520
If mornings like this are hard for you, subscribe and pray with us.

26
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:10,740
You were never meant to start them alone.

27
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:15,050
In the next few minutes, we are not asking God for one more thing.

28
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:22,480
We are asking him to open our eyes to mercy, grace, and the blessings that have been here the whole time.

29
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:26,110
Wherever you are, let us come to him together.

30
00:01:26,110 --> 00:01:28,620
His compassions never fail.

31
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:30,420
They are new every morning.

32
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:36,040
Read it again slowly, because there are three quiet things hidden in that sentence.

33
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,460
The first is this.

34
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:39,020
We are not consumed.

35
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:41,230
It does not say we were never hurt.

36
00:01:41,230 --> 00:01:43,190
It does not say nothing broke.

37
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:45,260
It says we were not finished off.

38
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:46,500
Something held.

39
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,800
Something carried us through a year we did not think we could carry.

40
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:53,000
That is not luck, and it is not our own strength.

41
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,430
The second is this.

42
00:01:54,430 --> 00:01:56,310
His compassions never fail.

43
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:59,940
Mercy does not thin out because it has been asked for too often.

44
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:03,330
There is no register in heaven where our name has appeared too many times.

45
00:02:03,330 --> 00:02:07,670
Nothing about us has ever worn you down, and nothing about us ever will.

46
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:10,530
And the third is the one we need most this morning.

47
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:11,960
New every morning.

48
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,490
Not warmed over.

49
00:02:13,490 --> 00:02:16,020
Not the portion left from yesterday.

50
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:19,720
God did not hand us the remainder of what we failed to use.

51
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:24,400
He opened something fresh while we were still asleep and unaware of it.

52
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,670
Lord, we have heard these words before.

53
00:02:26,670 --> 00:02:32,470
Many of us have read them on a wall, or on a card, or at the beginning of a hard year.

54
00:02:32,470 --> 00:02:35,910
Help us hear them this morning as if they were written for today.

55
00:02:35,910 --> 00:02:37,690
Not as a beautiful sentence.

56
00:02:37,690 --> 00:02:40,820
As something true about the room we are sitting in right now.

57
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:42,920
We are not going to rush past that.

58
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:48,540
Before we ask you for anything, we want to stay here a moment longer and simply agree with it.

59
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:50,000
Your love held us.

60
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,270
Your compassion did not fail.

61
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:55,880
And this morning arrived already carrying what it needed.

62
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:59,080
Which means the first thing worth saying is not a request.

63
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,720
It is a thank you.

64
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:02,450
Look at the light in the room.

65
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:04,360
It arrived without being asked.

66
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:06,520
Nobody negotiated for it.

67
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,720
Nobody earned it.

68
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:15,730
It simply came, the way it has come every day of your life, and most of those days you did not thank anyone for it.

69
00:03:15,730 --> 00:03:23,040
And it will be gone again tonight, and tomorrow it will come back, and you will not have asked for anything in return.

70
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:27,700
Psalm chapter one hundred three, verse two says,

71
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:32,050
Praise the Lord, my soul, and forget not all his benefits.

72
00:03:32,050 --> 00:03:34,260
Notice who is being spoken to there.

73
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,360
Not God.

74
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,710
Not other people.

75
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:41,930
The writer is talking to his own soul, because he knows it will not do this on its own.

76
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:44,260
Gratitude is not a feeling that shows up.

77
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:48,400
It is a direction we have to turn ourselves toward, sometimes firmly.

78
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:53,070
The way you would gently turn a child's face toward you so they can hear you.

79
00:03:53,070 --> 00:03:54,970
So this morning we are turning.

80
00:03:54,970 --> 00:04:00,194
Not because our hearts are full, but because you are worthy whether they are full or not.

81
00:04:00,194 --> 00:04:03,104
Heavenly Father, thank you for last night.

82
00:04:03,104 --> 00:04:04,874
Not for anything dramatic.

83
00:04:04,874 --> 00:04:09,884
For the ordinary fact that we lay down and lost consciousness for hours, and you did not.

84
00:04:09,884 --> 00:04:11,264
You do not sleep.

85
00:04:11,264 --> 00:04:20,744
So while we were unaware, unable to manage anything, unable to fix a single situation we had been worrying about all day, you kept watch.

86
00:04:20,744 --> 00:04:23,154
Thank you for the hours we cannot account for.

87
00:04:23,154 --> 00:04:27,014
Thank you that our worrying stopped and your working did not.

88
00:04:27,014 --> 00:04:29,744
We did not hold the world together while we slept.

89
00:04:29,744 --> 00:04:30,634
You did.

90
00:04:30,634 --> 00:04:32,974
And we woke to a morning we did not build.

91
00:04:32,974 --> 00:04:35,374
And thank you for the things that never happened.

92
00:04:35,374 --> 00:04:37,524
The accident we did not have.

93
00:04:37,524 --> 00:04:39,714
The phone call that did not come.

94
00:04:39,714 --> 00:04:45,554
We will never know what you kept away from us, because you did it quietly and did not tell us.

95
00:04:45,554 --> 00:04:49,734
We have spent years thanking you only for what arrived.

96
00:04:49,734 --> 00:04:52,584
Thank you for what never reached us.

97
00:04:52,584 --> 00:04:55,794
And thank you for something we almost never say out loud.

98
00:04:55,794 --> 00:04:59,354
Thank you for who you are, apart from anything you have done for us.

99
00:04:59,354 --> 00:05:03,774
If you had never answered a single prayer of ours, you would still be good.

100
00:05:03,774 --> 00:05:08,744
If nothing in our circumstances ever improves, you would still be faithful.

101
00:05:08,744 --> 00:05:16,094
We are so used to measuring you by our results that we forget you existed in perfect goodness before we needed anything.

102
00:05:16,094 --> 00:05:18,604
You are not kind because we are useful.

103
00:05:18,604 --> 00:05:21,074
You are kind because that is your nature.

104
00:05:21,074 --> 00:05:24,724
And before we say anything else, thank you for the cross.

105
00:05:24,724 --> 00:05:29,704
Everything we are about to pray this morning rests on a debt we could not pay and did not pay.

106
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,834
Mercy is not a mood you are in.

107
00:05:31,834 --> 00:05:33,374
It cost you something.

108
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:36,544
Let it never become ordinary to us that you came down.

109
00:05:36,544 --> 00:05:43,024
And yet, Father, if we are honest with you this morning, that is exactly what has happened.

110
00:05:43,024 --> 00:05:48,044
How many mornings have we been given, and how many did we actually receive?

111
00:05:48,044 --> 00:05:51,344
Father, we have to say something honest before we go any further.

112
00:05:51,344 --> 00:05:57,334
We have become people who are handed something extraordinary every single day and barely look up.

113
00:05:57,334 --> 00:06:00,104
We ate meals this week we cannot remember eating.

114
00:06:00,104 --> 00:06:04,454
We stood in a hot shower and thought about a problem the whole time.

115
00:06:04,454 --> 00:06:08,394
We drove a familiar road and arrived without remembering the drive.

116
00:06:08,394 --> 00:06:13,174
Someone spoke to us and we were physically present and completely absent.

117
00:06:13,174 --> 00:06:21,694
We counted what was missing before we counted anything we had, and we did it so automatically that it did not even feel like a choice.

118
00:06:21,694 --> 00:06:22,834
Forgive us.

119
00:06:22,834 --> 00:06:24,504
Not in a general way.

120
00:06:24,504 --> 00:06:31,464
Forgive us specifically, for the ingratitude we would never admit to anyone, because it does not look like sin.

121
00:06:31,464 --> 00:06:33,114
It looks like being busy.

122
00:06:33,114 --> 00:06:36,974
And Lord, there is a second thing, and it is heavier.

123
00:06:36,974 --> 00:06:39,874
Some of us feel guilty for not feeling grateful.

124
00:06:39,874 --> 00:06:42,394
We have tried to work up the emotion.

125
00:06:42,394 --> 00:06:45,154
We have told ourselves how much worse it could be.

126
00:06:45,154 --> 00:06:52,404
And the numbness did not move, and now we are ashamed of our own hearts on top of everything else.

127
00:06:52,404 --> 00:06:54,514
It is a strange kind of loneliness.

128
00:06:54,514 --> 00:06:55,564
Hear this.

129
00:06:55,564 --> 00:06:59,394
Your mercy did not arrive because we felt something.

130
00:06:59,394 --> 00:07:04,774
It was already new before we woke, before we had a single feeling about you at all.

131
00:07:04,774 --> 00:07:08,554
You do not wait at a distance until our hearts warm up.

132
00:07:08,554 --> 00:07:14,724
Because of your great love we are not consumed, and that was true this morning while we were still cold.

133
00:07:14,724 --> 00:07:16,994
So we are putting something down.

134
00:07:16,994 --> 00:07:18,334
Not our future.

135
00:07:18,334 --> 00:07:19,674
Not our people.

136
00:07:19,674 --> 00:07:20,764
Not the list.

137
00:07:20,764 --> 00:07:22,064
Just one thing.

138
00:07:22,064 --> 00:07:25,444
We are putting down the weight of having to hold all of it ourselves.

139
00:07:25,444 --> 00:07:32,114
The quiet belief that if we stop managing, calculating and bracing for one moment, everything will come apart.

140
00:07:32,114 --> 00:07:40,554
We have carried that so long we stopped noticing its weight, the way you stop noticing a bag you have worn all day until you finally set it down.

141
00:07:40,554 --> 00:07:42,214
We are setting it down now.

142
00:07:42,214 --> 00:07:44,944
We are not asking you to remove anything yet.

143
00:07:44,944 --> 00:07:49,854
We are simply admitting we are not the ones holding this together, and we never were.

144
00:07:49,854 --> 00:07:53,684
And into that honesty, Father, your mercy comes.

145
00:07:53,684 --> 00:07:56,534
It does not wait for us to be better first.

146
00:07:56,534 --> 00:07:58,444
Mercy does not run out.

147
00:07:58,444 --> 00:08:02,546
Say it again, because most of us do not actually believe it.

148
00:08:02,546 --> 00:08:04,796
Mercy does not run out.

149
00:08:04,796 --> 00:08:11,366
Father, there is a particular kind of tiredness that comes from failing at the same thing more than once.

150
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:13,286
It is not the failure itself.

151
00:08:13,286 --> 00:08:14,916
It is the repetition.

152
00:08:14,916 --> 00:08:18,036
The first time we came to you about it, we were broken.

153
00:08:18,036 --> 00:08:20,626
The tenth time, we were embarrassed.

154
00:08:20,626 --> 00:08:27,596
And somewhere after that we stopped bringing it at all, because we could not stand the sound of our own voice asking again.

155
00:08:27,596 --> 00:08:31,326
Some of us lost our temper with our children again this week.

156
00:08:31,326 --> 00:08:32,556
The same tone.

157
00:08:32,556 --> 00:08:35,956
The same regret afterward, standing in the hallway.

158
00:08:35,956 --> 00:08:42,786
Some of us broke a promise we made to ourselves in this very chair, at this very hour, not long ago.

159
00:08:42,786 --> 00:08:48,846
Some of us are carrying something nobody in our life knows about, and the worst part is not the thing itself.

160
00:08:48,846 --> 00:08:52,656
The worst part is that we know exactly how many times we have done it.

161
00:08:52,656 --> 00:08:58,036
And into that, your word says your compassions never fail.

162
00:08:58,036 --> 00:08:59,536
Never fail.

163
00:08:59,536 --> 00:09:01,356
Not they last a long time.

164
00:09:01,356 --> 00:09:03,616
Not they stretch further than most.

165
00:09:03,616 --> 00:09:04,916
They do not fail.

166
00:09:04,916 --> 00:09:07,276
There is no number at which they stop.

167
00:09:07,276 --> 00:09:14,886
We have been quietly assuming mercy works like patience, and that we have been drawing down a supply that must be nearly gone by now.

168
00:09:14,886 --> 00:09:16,456
That is not what you said.

169
00:09:16,456 --> 00:09:17,726
You said new.

170
00:09:17,726 --> 00:09:18,846
Every morning.

171
00:09:18,846 --> 00:09:25,276
Which means the mercy available to us this morning has never been touched, because it did not exist yesterday.

172
00:09:25,276 --> 00:09:28,256
This is the difference between mercy and endurance.

173
00:09:28,256 --> 00:09:29,996
Endurance wears thin.

174
00:09:29,996 --> 00:09:38,256
It is a finite thing being stretched, and everyone who has ever loved a difficult person knows the feeling of it running low.

175
00:09:38,256 --> 00:09:40,936
Your compassion is not being stretched.

176
00:09:40,936 --> 00:09:42,546
It is being renewed.

177
00:09:42,546 --> 00:09:44,846
Nothing in you is being used up by us.

178
00:09:44,846 --> 00:09:46,106
So we come.

179
00:09:46,106 --> 00:09:48,316
Not with a better argument than last time.

180
00:09:48,316 --> 00:09:55,166
Not with a promise to do better, because we have offered those before and you were not impressed by them then either.

181
00:09:55,166 --> 00:09:57,796
We come the only way anyone has ever come to you.

182
00:09:57,796 --> 00:10:00,486
Empty-handed, and welcome anyway.

183
00:10:00,486 --> 00:10:02,766
And we can say that for one reason only.

184
00:10:02,766 --> 00:10:07,676
Not because we are sorry enough, but because Jesus already carried it.

185
00:10:07,676 --> 00:10:10,506
It was already settled at the cross long before this morning.

186
00:10:10,506 --> 00:10:13,916
Mercy is not you overlooking what we did.

187
00:10:13,916 --> 00:10:16,226
It is you having paid for it.

188
00:10:16,226 --> 00:10:17,276
Meet us here.

189
00:10:17,276 --> 00:10:20,136
Not at the version of us we are hoping to become.

190
00:10:20,136 --> 00:10:22,606
Here, at the version that failed again.

191
00:10:22,606 --> 00:10:24,876
And Father, do something further.

192
00:10:24,876 --> 00:10:28,876
Whatever mercy we receive this morning, let it not stop with us.

193
00:10:28,876 --> 00:10:33,576
There is someone we will see today who has failed us in a way we have not released.

194
00:10:33,576 --> 00:10:36,176
Give us enough of your mercy that we can spare some.

195
00:10:36,176 --> 00:10:39,116
Let us be as slow with them as you have been with us.

196
00:10:39,116 --> 00:10:41,526
But mercy is not the whole of it.

197
00:10:41,526 --> 00:10:44,226
Mercy keeps us from being consumed.

198
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:46,566
Mercy deals with what is behind us.

199
00:10:46,566 --> 00:10:51,356
And in a few hours we will be standing in front of something we do not have the strength for.

200
00:10:51,356 --> 00:10:54,116
For that, we need something else.

201
00:10:54,116 --> 00:10:57,766
There is something on today's schedule that we are not strong enough for.

202
00:10:57,766 --> 00:10:59,986
Most of us know exactly what it is.

203
00:10:59,986 --> 00:11:02,146
We knew before we opened our eyes.

204
00:11:02,146 --> 00:11:06,876
A conversation we have rehearsed four times and still cannot start.

205
00:11:06,876 --> 00:11:11,686
A room we have to walk into where we are the only one who will say the hard thing.

206
00:11:11,686 --> 00:11:13,636
A drive we have to make alone.

207
00:11:13,636 --> 00:11:18,786
A person at home who needs another day of care from us, and we gave everything we had yesterday.

208
00:11:18,786 --> 00:11:20,916
Or it is nothing dramatic at all.

209
00:11:20,916 --> 00:11:30,266
It is the same work, the same hours, the same tasks we have done a thousand times, and somewhere along the way we stopped being able to find the point of it.

210
00:11:30,266 --> 00:11:33,216
Second Corinthians chapter twelve, verse nine.

211
00:11:33,216 --> 00:11:38,346
My grace is sufficient for you, for my power is made perfect in weakness.

212
00:11:38,346 --> 00:11:44,256
Father, we want to be careful with that verse, because Paul did not write it after you fixed his problem.

213
00:11:44,256 --> 00:11:49,076
He asked you three times to take something away, and you did not take it away.

214
00:11:49,076 --> 00:11:54,126
What he received instead was you, in the middle of it, and he called that better.

215
00:11:54,126 --> 00:11:57,366
So we are not going to ask for an easier day.

216
00:11:57,366 --> 00:12:01,566
We are asking for grace to be sufficient for the day we actually have.

217
00:12:01,566 --> 00:12:03,602
And we notice the word you chose.

218
00:12:03,602 --> 00:12:04,722
Sufficient.

219
00:12:04,722 --> 00:12:06,092
Not abundant.

220
00:12:06,092 --> 00:12:07,612
Not overflowing.

221
00:12:07,612 --> 00:12:08,502
Enough.

222
00:12:08,502 --> 00:12:13,082
Grace usually arrives at the exact size of the next step and not one inch further.

223
00:12:13,082 --> 00:12:15,692
That is uncomfortable for people like us.

224
00:12:15,692 --> 00:12:19,082
We would rather see the whole staircase before we move.

225
00:12:19,082 --> 00:12:23,762
But it means we will never be handed more than we need and left to manage it alone.

226
00:12:23,762 --> 00:12:29,782
It means the strength for eleven o'clock will be there at eleven o'clock, and not at seven.

227
00:12:29,782 --> 00:12:31,752
That is not you withholding.

228
00:12:31,752 --> 00:12:34,072
That is you keeping us close.

229
00:12:34,072 --> 00:12:41,052
So give us grace that is still patient by the afternoon, not only in the first quiet hour of the day.

230
00:12:41,052 --> 00:12:46,812
Make us kind when we are depleted, because anyone can be kind when they are rested.

231
00:12:46,812 --> 00:12:51,332
Hold us to a promise we made back when we had more energy than we have now.

232
00:12:51,332 --> 00:12:56,852
And let us do ordinary work faithfully when nobody notices and nothing about it feels significant.

233
00:12:56,852 --> 00:13:00,422
And where we are weakest today, do not make us strong.

234
00:13:00,422 --> 00:13:01,992
Make yourself evident.

235
00:13:01,992 --> 00:13:05,702
Let somebody see something in us that we know is not ours.

236
00:13:05,702 --> 00:13:07,682
And if we fail at it anyway.

237
00:13:07,682 --> 00:13:11,212
If we hear ourselves saying the thing we swore we would not say.

238
00:13:11,212 --> 00:13:14,092
Do not let us decide that the morning was wasted.

239
00:13:14,092 --> 00:13:16,542
Your grace was still sufficient.

240
00:13:16,542 --> 00:13:18,722
We just met the end of ours first.

241
00:13:18,722 --> 00:13:20,442
But there is one more thing.

242
00:13:20,442 --> 00:13:28,222
We keep asking you for strength to face what is coming, and we have not once stopped to notice what is already in our hands.

243
00:13:28,222 --> 00:13:31,792
There is a glass of water within reach of most of us right now.

244
00:13:31,792 --> 00:13:33,542
We poured it without a thought.

245
00:13:33,542 --> 00:13:38,242
Clean and safe, in the amount we wanted, at the temperature we wanted.

246
00:13:38,242 --> 00:13:41,362
It arrives through a wall in our home whenever we ask for it.

247
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:49,642
For most of human history, and for a great many people alive this morning, that single glass would have been the most valuable object in the room.

248
00:13:49,642 --> 00:13:51,682
Father, we did not see it.

249
00:13:51,682 --> 00:13:58,352
James chapter one, verse seventeen says every good and perfect gift is from above.

250
00:13:58,352 --> 00:13:59,442
Every one.

251
00:13:59,442 --> 00:14:00,972
Not the rare ones.

252
00:14:00,972 --> 00:14:04,992
Not the ones that arrive after long prayer and finally make us cry.

253
00:14:04,992 --> 00:14:12,582
Every good thing in our lives came down from you, including the ones so constant that we stopped registering them as gifts at all.

254
00:14:12,582 --> 00:14:16,432
This is our real request this morning, and it is the one we came for.

255
00:14:16,432 --> 00:14:17,942
Open our eyes.

256
00:14:17,942 --> 00:14:19,582
Not to something new.

257
00:14:19,582 --> 00:14:21,312
To what is already here.

258
00:14:21,312 --> 00:14:24,162
Let us hear it right now, before we go anywhere.

259
00:14:24,162 --> 00:14:28,382
Somewhere in this house there is the sound of another person moving.

260
00:14:28,382 --> 00:14:29,862
We are not alone in the world.

261
00:14:29,862 --> 00:14:35,652
Our body is breathing without being told to, and it has done that our whole lives without a single instruction from us.

262
00:14:35,652 --> 00:14:39,382
There is a key in our pocket, and a door somewhere that opens for us.

263
00:14:39,382 --> 00:14:43,792
There is a name in our phone we could call at a bad hour and they would answer.

264
00:14:43,792 --> 00:14:47,082
There is food in the kitchen that we did not worry about yesterday.

265
00:14:47,082 --> 00:14:51,092
There is a pair of shoes that fit us, and somewhere to be today.

266
00:14:51,092 --> 00:14:54,612
Some of us are praying beside someone we once begged you for.

267
00:14:54,612 --> 00:14:56,582
We asked for them for years.

268
00:14:56,582 --> 00:15:01,562
They are here, in the next room, and we have not thanked you for them in months.

269
00:15:01,562 --> 00:15:04,842
We have been treating all of that as the background.

270
00:15:04,842 --> 00:15:07,322
As the setting the story happens in.

271
00:15:07,322 --> 00:15:09,092
It is not the setting, Father.

272
00:15:09,092 --> 00:15:10,492
It is the story.

273
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:17,252
It is you, providing, continuously, in a way so steady that it became invisible.

274
00:15:17,252 --> 00:15:20,542
And forgive us for what we have made the word blessing mean.

275
00:15:20,542 --> 00:15:23,112
We have made it mean the thing we do not have yet.

276
00:15:23,112 --> 00:15:25,022
The answer that is still coming.

277
00:15:25,022 --> 00:15:31,342
We have been standing in the middle of an answered prayer we prayed five years ago, complaining about a different one.

278
00:15:31,342 --> 00:15:33,652
We are not asking for more this morning.

279
00:15:33,652 --> 00:15:35,352
We are asking for sight.

280
00:15:35,352 --> 00:15:38,122
Give us eyes for what is already here.

281
00:15:38,122 --> 00:15:47,342
Let us walk through this ordinary day and keep catching ourselves noticing, not because any of it is impressive, but because all of it is yours.

282
00:15:47,342 --> 00:15:50,462
And when we start seeing it, do not let us hold it.

283
00:15:50,462 --> 00:15:56,922
Because we are not the only ones in this house, on this street, or in this hour who need something from you.

284
00:15:56,922 --> 00:16:03,022
Somewhere this morning, someone is awake and cannot find one single thing to be thankful for.

285
00:16:03,022 --> 00:16:04,766
They are not being difficult.

286
00:16:04,766 --> 00:16:05,796
They have looked.

287
00:16:05,796 --> 00:16:08,206
Father, we are praying for them now.

288
00:16:08,206 --> 00:16:16,036
Not that their situation would suddenly reverse, but that before this day is over you would give them one thing.

289
00:16:16,036 --> 00:16:16,866
One.

290
00:16:16,866 --> 00:16:18,966
Small enough to be believable.

291
00:16:18,966 --> 00:16:21,536
A stranger who is kind for no reason.

292
00:16:21,536 --> 00:16:23,586
A few minutes where the pressure lifts.

293
00:16:23,586 --> 00:16:27,246
Something ordinary that lands like it was placed there on purpose.

294
00:16:27,246 --> 00:16:35,126
Give them a single crack of light, and give them the ability to see it when it comes, because the seeing is the harder half.

295
00:16:35,126 --> 00:16:36,196
We know.

296
00:16:36,196 --> 00:16:37,366
We were there.

297
00:16:37,366 --> 00:16:42,276
And Father, we bring you the ones who have been waiting a long time.

298
00:16:42,276 --> 00:16:47,056
They have prayed the same prayer so many times that the words have gone flat in their mouth.

299
00:16:47,056 --> 00:16:52,026
The answer has not come, and worse, no explanation has come either.

300
00:16:52,026 --> 00:16:58,806
We are not going to pretend to know your timing, and we are not going to hand them a slogan this morning.

301
00:16:58,806 --> 00:17:02,306
But we ask you for something specific for them.

302
00:17:02,306 --> 00:17:08,156
Give them the ability to be thankful while they are still waiting, which is the hardest gratitude there is.

303
00:17:08,156 --> 00:17:09,966
Not thankful for the delay.

304
00:17:09,966 --> 00:17:11,156
Thankful in it.

305
00:17:11,156 --> 00:17:14,466
Let them find you good before they find you finished.

306
00:17:14,466 --> 00:17:17,446
There is another group, and we hold them gently.

307
00:17:17,446 --> 00:17:19,526
Some who hear this have lost someone.

308
00:17:19,526 --> 00:17:30,226
And a strange guilt has attached itself to them, because there are moments in the day when they laugh, or enjoy the sun, or forget for an hour, and then it feels like a betrayal.

309
00:17:30,226 --> 00:17:32,246
Father, tell them it is not.

310
00:17:32,246 --> 00:17:35,306
Gratitude is not disloyalty to grief.

311
00:17:35,306 --> 00:17:36,606
They can hold both.

312
00:17:36,606 --> 00:17:41,966
You are near to the brokenhearted, and you are not standing over them waiting for them to cheer up.

313
00:17:41,966 --> 00:17:43,646
Sit with them this morning.

314
00:17:43,646 --> 00:17:48,846
Let them weep and let them be thankful in the same hour, and let neither one cancel the other.

315
00:17:48,846 --> 00:17:52,076
And there are the ones who are keeping someone else alive this morning.

316
00:17:52,076 --> 00:17:53,156
A parent.

317
00:17:53,156 --> 00:17:54,296
A husband.

318
00:17:54,296 --> 00:17:56,356
A daughter who moved back home.

319
00:17:56,356 --> 00:18:00,856
They get up before they are ready, every day, and nobody claps.

320
00:18:00,856 --> 00:18:04,946
Father, they have been giving from a place that has nothing left in it.

321
00:18:04,946 --> 00:18:07,216
Carry the part of it they cannot carry.

322
00:18:07,216 --> 00:18:10,726
And let somebody thank them today in a way they can actually hear.

323
00:18:10,726 --> 00:18:13,016
And last, our own homes.

324
00:18:13,016 --> 00:18:19,666
The people we live with have become the most familiar thing in our lives, which is exactly why we stopped seeing them.

325
00:18:19,666 --> 00:18:20,786
Forgive us.

326
00:18:20,786 --> 00:18:25,656
Let gratitude be spoken out loud in our houses today, not only felt.

327
00:18:25,656 --> 00:18:31,886
Let us tell one person specifically what we are glad for about them, and not in general terms.

328
00:18:31,886 --> 00:18:36,026
Make our home a place where good things get named instead of assumed.

329
00:18:36,026 --> 00:18:39,296
And now, Father, bring all of this back to us.

330
00:18:39,296 --> 00:18:44,606
Because everything we have just asked for other people is something we have to choose for ourselves first.

331
00:18:44,606 --> 00:18:48,596
I want to stop saying we for a moment, and speak only for myself.

332
00:18:48,596 --> 00:18:52,346
I choose to count what I have been given before I count what I am missing.

333
00:18:52,346 --> 00:18:54,406
That list was there when I woke up.

334
00:18:54,406 --> 00:18:55,806
It is still there.

335
00:18:55,806 --> 00:18:58,916
Nothing on it has been solved while we have been praying.

336
00:18:58,916 --> 00:19:04,366
But it is no longer the first thing I see, and I am not handing it the first hour of my day again.

337
00:19:04,366 --> 00:19:12,876
I choose to walk into today as someone who has already received more than I asked for, rather than someone still waiting to be paid.

338
00:19:12,876 --> 00:19:16,946
And I will thank you today even if today changes nothing.

339
00:19:16,946 --> 00:19:18,206
That is the harder one.

340
00:19:18,206 --> 00:19:20,216
If the phone does not ring.

341
00:19:20,216 --> 00:19:22,496
If the answer does not come.

342
00:19:22,496 --> 00:19:32,826
If this evening looks exactly like last evening and the thing I have been carrying is still sitting there at the end of it, I will still say that your mercy was new this morning, because it was.

343
00:19:32,826 --> 00:19:36,116
My gratitude is not a receipt for services rendered.

344
00:19:36,116 --> 00:19:39,246
I am not thankful because the situation improved.

345
00:19:39,246 --> 00:19:46,526
I am thankful because you are who you said you are, and that was settled long before my circumstances got involved.

346
00:19:46,526 --> 00:19:50,736
And then there is this, and it is the thing I most want to say.

347
00:19:50,736 --> 00:19:55,436
Lord, I have spent a long time wanting things from you.

348
00:19:55,436 --> 00:19:57,966
Mercy, so I can be clean.

349
00:19:57,966 --> 00:20:00,376
Grace, so I can be strong.

350
00:20:00,376 --> 00:20:03,346
Blessings, so my life can be full.

351
00:20:03,346 --> 00:20:07,514
All of that is good, and you offer all of it freely.

352
00:20:07,514 --> 00:20:09,214
But this morning I want you.

353
00:20:09,214 --> 00:20:10,504
More than mercy.

354
00:20:10,504 --> 00:20:11,914
More than grace.

355
00:20:11,914 --> 00:20:14,714
More than every good thing that comes down from you.

356
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:16,494
I want the One they come from.

357
00:20:16,494 --> 00:20:18,734
Not the gifts arriving from your hand.

358
00:20:18,734 --> 00:20:19,774
Your face.

359
00:20:19,774 --> 00:20:25,724
Because it is entirely possible to love what God provides and slowly stop loving God.

360
00:20:25,724 --> 00:20:31,494
I do not want to find out one day that I have been in love with the provision all along.

361
00:20:31,494 --> 00:20:36,574
I have prayed to you for years the way I would text someone I only contact when I need something.

362
00:20:36,574 --> 00:20:38,134
I am not proud of that.

363
00:20:38,134 --> 00:20:40,934
I do not know how to fix it in one morning.

364
00:20:40,934 --> 00:20:47,374
But I want to want you, and I am saying it plainly, in case wanting to want you is where it starts.

365
00:20:47,374 --> 00:20:51,624
If I had everything I have prayed for and did not have you, I would have nothing.

366
00:20:51,624 --> 00:20:54,994
If I have you and nothing else ever changes, I have enough.

367
00:20:54,994 --> 00:21:01,294
And I can only say any of this because you chose me first, on a morning when I was not looking for you at all.

368
00:21:01,294 --> 00:21:02,734
So take this day.

369
00:21:02,734 --> 00:21:08,254
It is not much, and it is not particularly impressive, but it is all of it.

370
00:21:08,254 --> 00:21:09,604
I choose you.

371
00:21:09,604 --> 00:21:15,014
This morning, and at eleven o'clock when it is harder, and tonight when nobody is watching.

372
00:21:15,014 --> 00:21:16,384
I choose you.

373
00:21:16,384 --> 00:21:21,914
Because of the Lord's great love we are not consumed, for his compassions never fail.

374
00:21:21,914 --> 00:21:23,394
They are new every morning.

375
00:21:23,394 --> 00:21:24,824
Great is your faithfulness.

376
00:21:24,824 --> 00:21:26,854
That was true before we prayed.

377
00:21:26,854 --> 00:21:30,864
It will still be true tomorrow, when we have forgotten it again.

378
00:21:30,864 --> 00:21:32,554
The list is still there.

379
00:21:32,554 --> 00:21:34,694
We are not pretending otherwise.

380
00:21:34,694 --> 00:21:39,624
But we picked up something else first this morning, and we are carrying that out the door with us.

381
00:21:39,624 --> 00:21:42,594
That we were held through a night we did not manage.

382
00:21:42,594 --> 00:21:46,534
That we were met with mercy we had already used many times.

383
00:21:46,534 --> 00:21:49,854
That grace will arrive at exactly the size of the next step.

384
00:21:49,854 --> 00:21:54,384
And that we have been surrounded the whole time by good things we had stopped seeing.

385
00:21:54,384 --> 00:21:58,434
Nothing in our circumstances has changed in the last half hour.

386
00:21:58,434 --> 00:22:00,254
Something in our eyes has.

387
00:22:00,254 --> 00:22:02,284
We will forget this by lunch.

388
00:22:02,284 --> 00:22:03,514
That is alright.

389
00:22:03,514 --> 00:22:05,094
Forgetting is not failing.

390
00:22:05,094 --> 00:22:10,784
We will come back tomorrow and let it be new again, because that is the one thing it is guaranteed to be.

391
00:22:10,784 --> 00:22:17,414
We choose to walk into this day as people who have already received, not people still waiting to begin.

392
00:22:17,414 --> 00:22:19,434
Father, send us out.

393
00:22:19,434 --> 00:22:22,844
May mercy reach you before the news does today.

394
00:22:22,844 --> 00:22:28,194
May grace be enough for you in the exact place you already know you are not enough.

395
00:22:28,194 --> 00:22:34,454
And may your eyes keep opening, again and again, to what has been in front of you the whole time.

396
00:22:34,454 --> 00:22:39,624
May you become someone who notices, and who says it out loud.

397
00:22:39,624 --> 00:22:45,454
May you be hard to discourage, because you have learned to count what is already in your hands.

398
00:22:45,454 --> 00:22:47,424
In the name of Jesus we pray.

399
00:22:47,424 --> 00:22:48,374
Amen.

400
00:22:48,374 --> 00:22:50,714
Before you go, one small thing.

401
00:22:50,714 --> 00:22:52,784
Type one word in the comments.

402
00:22:52,784 --> 00:22:55,684
One thing you are thankful for this morning.

403
00:22:55,684 --> 00:22:56,994
Just one word.

404
00:22:56,994 --> 00:23:02,184
Then read a few of the others, because someone down there is going to need to borrow yours today.

405
00:23:02,184 --> 00:23:10,843
If this helped you start the morning differently, send it to the person you thought of when we prayed for those who could not find anything to be thankful for.

406
00:23:10,843 --> 00:23:14,923
Leaving a like helps this prayer reach someone waking up alone with their list.

407
00:23:14,923 --> 00:23:20,233
And if you want to keep beginning your days like this, subscribe, and we will meet you here tomorrow.

408
00:23:20,233 --> 00:23:21,463
One last thing.

409
00:23:21,463 --> 00:23:24,323
Gratitude is not meant to keep us in the room.

410
00:23:24,323 --> 00:23:26,253
It sends us out the door.

411
00:23:26,253 --> 00:23:32,673
And the day waiting on the other side of that door has things in it we cannot see yet, and cannot carry on our own.

412
00:23:32,673 --> 00:23:36,123
That is the next prayer, and it is already on your screen.

413
00:23:36,123 --> 00:23:39,753
It will be waiting for you whenever you are ready.
